From a9a04651fd1239d4a32b2d909a81d514566ba49a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viswanath Kraleti <viswanath.kraleti@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:52:32 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] platforms/nord-rrd: replace ddr_a/ddr_b with DDR tuning
 partitions

Nord DDR firmware needs dedicated storage for DDR training and SED
(eye-margin detection) data. The legacy ddr_a/ddr_b partitions are no
longer used, so drop them and add the following partitions to the UFS
OTP LUN (LUN3), all sized in multiples of 128KB as LUN3 requires:

- ddr_training_{A,B,factory}: runtime DDR training/calibration results
- ddr_training_golden_{A,B}, ddr_training_factory_golden: golden copies
  used to integrity-check the stored training parameters
- ddr_buffer_e_{A,B,factory}, ddr_buffer_i_{A,B,factory}: SED Buffer E
  and Buffer I storage
- ddr_debug_{A,B}: DDR debug/DDI output

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Viswanath Kraleti <viswanath.kraleti@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/qcom-ptool/pull/207]
---
